A||N||27||Haze_Performance||Someone please explain this to me...||||5||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-13-2001||01:51 AM||||Now I want to first say...Im not knocking ANYONE who has done this...I just want to know why..<P>I see tons of Fieros for sale that are all kit-ed up. Ferrari,Lambo...ect..And the ads they always say that the car is "Amazing, Drop dead gorgeous ect... And it cost 20/30/40/50+ grand to complete. Why do most of the people leave the Fiero V6 engine in it?? It seems quite silly to me that you spend so much money making a Fiero look just like a Ferrari, & you leave the engine. Why not spend the extra $4000 and put in a small block to back it up alittle. I would feel VERY stupid if I had a exact 355 look a like & a Honda pulled up next to me at the light. The next thing ya know...Zoooooom the Honda smokes me....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I met a guy at the gas station in a Lambo kit on a 84 coupe. He told me he spent $22,000 on the kit (w/labor). It looked great but it still had the L4 in it. He said.. "I wish I had more money to swap in a V6 or a small block.. Come on!!! $22,000 on the looks of the car, without any H.P. to back it up??<P>I would rather have $22,000 invested in a stock looking Fiero than one thats just looks. For that kinda cash you can out handle & power any car on the road.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ok Im done now...!!!!Flame Suit On!!!! <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||pHoOl||03-13-2001||02:03 AM||||Moo!!!!<P><BR>I agree with you though.  When you're spending that much, what's an extra for or five G's to put in an LT1 with twin turbos or something?<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who can't outrun the cops.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||03-13-2001||02:34 AM||||i totally agree. what makes it really bad is when they keep the 2.5 auto and keep the interior stock. just stupid.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||03-13-2001||02:41 AM||||Unfortunately, from the kits that I have seen, (and I have only seen the kits in the Southern California area, others maybe different...) I have only seen a FEW kits that were not outright butchering of decent Fieros. Im talking about the full bore Diablo and Ferrari F40 body conversions. I have seen some neat GT-40 kits and Finale styles but the chassis altering kits make my skin crawl!<P>The Kit Cars that have impressed me are the ones that aren't afraid to lift the hood. Not hesitant to see the engine. It shows attention to detail from the company and sometimes the owner that is not very common. The kit cars that I have seen and have crawled under and worked on have been nothing but electrical, mechanical and engineering nightmares with only a FEW exceptions.<P>Fieros that have been stretched out with only the minimal welding on the extensions, Fieros that have sloppy fiberglass bodies somehow fastened on with sheetmetal screws to flimsy brackets, household electrical connectors holding onto loose wires to power the various lights...ad nauseum. Some of those with these Diablos and some Ferraris are spending as much as they would spend on the real thing just to make it work right.<P>Why don't they get a big engine and soup up their hot looking cars?<P>Some of them are spending a lot of money just trying to make it dependable...<P>Others are happy with the kit that they have because they did not have delusions of granduer and had not only the realistic aspirations of what they wanted out of their Fiero/Kit Car but they also knew what they could realisticly do to their Fiero.<P>Thats my opinion and I reserve the right to be completely wrong. <P>&gt;:P<P>Okay Haze, now that I have all flame throwers aimed at me....RUN!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||03-13-2001||02:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B><BR>Okay Haze, now that I have all flame throwers aimed at me....RUN!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">... Dont worry Ill stand behind you(WAY BEHIND hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery (Updated Weekly)</A>||||reg||14
Z||000005||KRMFiero||03-13-2001||07:21 AM||||well its gonna suck for him when someone pulls up beside him and wants to race, the I4 isnt that fast by it self, with the body kit on it it probley wieghs more so it will probley be even slower hehe<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||03-13-2001||07:38 AM||||To some, looks are more important than performance. Not that they wouldn't like to have a high HP motor but, to some, that's just not as important as "the look". And, if your buiding it to impress the opposite sex, well, it's hard to make an impression with a faded paint job and ragged interior even if there's a LT1 lurking under the hood. And, after all, if your cruising down the highway at 50-70 MPH, it's had to tell if it's an L-4 or a V-12.<P>Other questions I would like answers to: <BR>Why do some kids paint their motor yellow if the body is not?<BR>Why do they put performance stickers on a Civic?<BR>Why do some like the wheels sticking out beyond the wheelwells?<BR>Etc, etc, etc.<P>Personally, I like the the way the stock GT body looks. I would rather put my money into a motor and suspension and keep the body close to stock. That way, when some puke in a Honda eggs me into a race, he has to admit he go beat by a FIERO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> and not some exotic high dollar car.<P>Don't get me wrong. I like SOME re-bodys but, there are only a couple I would ever consider doing. Of course, that's after I have a "kit butt" motor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Oreif||03-13-2001||09:37 AM||||I agree, If you've got +$20,000 to dump into a body kit, why not upgrade the mechanical side? I could see someone using the V-6 for a while until the motor is ready or even using the V-6 with a lot of upgrades, But the I4?!? There is a guy on Ebay selling a Fiero/testarossa car. It has the original I4 in it. I think one of the reasons they keep the original engines might be that if they bought a "turn-key" kit car, the manufacturer<BR>may have left the chassis/mechanics the same to keep the cost down for selling purposes.<BR>But if you are building it yourself, why not do the upgrades first before you put the body on?||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||03-13-2001||09:54 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B><BR>Other questions I would like answers to: <BR>Why do some kids paint their motor yellow if the body is not?<BR>Why do they put performance stickers on a Civic?<BR>Why do some like the wheels sticking out beyond the wheelwells?<BR>Etc, etc, etc.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Answers<BR>1) As someone who put no tiny amount into powdercoating the pretty red parts of my engine yellow, I feel well suited to answer this question.<BR>Cuz it looks nice. Why should the car be yellow to justify a colorful engine? All Fieros aren't red. Why should all the engines be red? My yellow engine never fails to attract attention whenever I pop the hood. Please don't defend some gold chain wearing middle aged divorced guy driving a 4 cylinder Lambo just to get some trim in one sentance, then criticize me in another. That's just creepy.<BR>2) For Christ's sake, why the consistent hammering on Civics? They are so damn ubiquitous because they might actually be decent cars. Why not be original and use "Kia"" or "Daewoo" once in a while? An overabundance of decals on any car that is not used for motorsports is a bit silly.  But ease up on Hondas. It's getting old.<BR>3) Again, cuz the driver likes it. I can't explain why someone would like the skated look, but until someone breaks into your garage and does it to your car, quit trippin.<P>Sorry if I unloaded both barrels on ya Mrfixit, but I like my Old Yellar.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=258191&a=1921599&p=16712481&Sequence=5"> <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||03-13-2001||10:43 AM||||A manager that I usta work for (he's no longer with the company) had an unspoken rule: <P><B>"An ounce of appearance is worth a pound of performance."</B><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||10:55 AM||||not taking this as a flame. I like the looks of the exotics, not necessarily their performance. After all the 'legal' speedlimit anywhere almost in us is 70 mph. I could have easily bought a used real 308 for less than $25K. But with that you have the $5 K a year maintainence. This way I got a car thats fun to drive, nice looking and I can get parts at K-Mart. I wanted reliability, is why I didnt go the enormous V8 swap, basicly it all stock, no modifing wiring etc. With the bolt in engine conversion and the turbocharger I got small block performance anyway. V8 real Ferraris have a sound all there own too, and a hopped up V6 sounds more like it than a Caddy or Chevy V8. Anyone whos heard a real Ferrari knows what I mean---a swarm of angry bees. Anyway, if I wanted a race car that really performed, Id have kept it stock and built up a super powertrain. But just for the looks and fun and attending car shows and cruises it really dont even matter if it runs at all, just to get to where your going. I know what you guys are all saying and I respect that too. Just for the record I think that the wheels sticking 6'' from fender is totally stupid looking, cant help but laugh out loud when I see one. Also lot of you spend fortunes on Stero systems. If I want to hear music its far cheaper and more enjoyable to sit at home sipping beer and listening. I seldom even turn my radio on at all. If I pop the face off at a parking lot sometimes forget to even put it back on for weeks. So-----you guys all enjoy your drag racing, booming radios, and Ill just enjoy my ride in the country.<P>Oh yea forgot, I have way more fun in my kitcar with no payments than Id have paying for a $28,000 Taurus.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||03-13-2001||11:40 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>not taking this as a flame. I like the looks of the exotics, not necessarily their performance. After all the 'legal' speedlimit anywhere almost in us is 70 mph. I could have easily bought a used real 308 for less than $25K. But with that you have the $5 K a year maintainence. This way I got a car thats fun to drive, nice looking and I can get parts at K-Mart. I wanted reliability, is why I didnt go the enormous V8 swap, basicly it all stock, no modifing wiring etc. With the bolt in engine conversion and the turbocharger I got small block performance anyway. V8 real Ferraris have a sound all there own too, and a hopped up V6 sounds more like it than a Caddy or Chevy V8. Anyone whos heard a real Ferrari knows what I mean---a swarm of angry bees. Anyway, if I wanted a race car that really performed, Id have kept it stock and built up a super powertrain. But just for the looks and fun and attending car shows and cruises it really dont even matter if it runs at all, just to get to where your going. I know what you guys are all saying and I respect that too. Just for the record I think that the wheels sticking 6'' from fender is totally stupid looking, cant help but laugh out loud when I see one. Also lot of you spend fortunes on Stero systems. If I want to hear music its far cheaper and more enjoyable to sit at home sipping beer and listening. I seldom even turn my radio on at all. If I pop the face off at a parking lot sometimes forget to even put it back on for weeks. So-----you guys all enjoy your drag racing, booming radios, and Ill just enjoy my ride in the country.<P>Oh yea forgot, I have way more fun in my kitcar with no payments than Id have paying for a $28,000 Taurus.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey rogergarrison..<BR>  This was at no way directed at you...I love your car. Im just talking about the guys that spend 10's of thousands of dollars to make a Fiero look like a Ferrari in every way, & then kust leave the engine..<P>----------------------------------------------<P><B>stimpy,<BR> Im not knocking Hondas.. Some of them are quite quick..(Quicker than Camaro's & Mustangs :( ) Your right about the Honda being picked on. Its been a good car since the 70's here in the US. When are people going to give it its props?........ :D </B>||||reg||14
Z||000012||danny boy||03-13-2001||07:39 PM||||Stupid Hondas...Why do we even have those junky little econocans over here on our shores? I mean, do we even need any other cars than what comes from Detroit?Why would Anyone want a car that is cheap,fairly easy to work on,and easy to find parts for? Who cares about gas milage and reliability? Personally, I think we should all write a letter to congress asking that they ban Hondas,no, ALL import cars from this country.<BR>              Sorry, couldn't resist.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000013||Galen||03-13-2001||07:50 PM||||They should ban your 'GTO' from this country too? <P>And Fiero's did not come from Detriot, they came from Pontiac.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||08:46 PM||||I didnt take offense, I was just making the point why some of us care more for the look, not the performance as much. I just stated why 'I' did mine the way I did. I figure with time and everything that I bought along the way is probably in the vicinity of $25,000 myself. The time is worth something. In actual cash outlay i got approx $1500 in chassis (86 SE w/40k) $2500 for my body kit, $4,000 in drivetrain, $3500 in wheels n tires, $300 in emblems etc, about $1,000 in my interior, $400 in suspension upgrades, $500 in brakes, maybe $1,000 in dumb misc crap like speedo, shifter, etc. Figure my labor, paint makes the differnce. And its essentially a new car....with no payments.||||reg||1
Z||000015||danny boy||03-13-2001||10:13 PM||||Yeah, especially my GTO!  <P>  No, seriously, Some people want nice cars but don't feel the need for a car with a lot of power.As strange as it may seem to me,I know a few people who want the look but don't like to drive fast or want a fast car. They just want it to look that way. My GT is just for looks.It is and will be stock mechanically.Hopefully it will look really nice soon and will turn heads,but when I feel the need to act like Shumacher I've got another car for that.||||reg||1
Z||000016||WKDFIRO||03-13-2001||11:34 PM||||Uuuuhhhh...some of those Hondas are here on our shores because they make them here, on our shores...east shore...Honda has a factory that makes Accords in North Carolina I think...Mitsubishi made your Stealth but I don't think they made it here on our shores...<P>Really Im trying not to laugh....<P>Stimpy, I like the V6 HO emblem on your plenum!<P>LOL...Danny you are too funny!||||reg||11
Z||000017||Rodney||03-14-2001||01:09 AM||||I have had my 88 Mera for 6-7 years now. I have never had anyone try to race me. They all succumb to the Ferrari mystique. Porches, Corvettes, superbikes. They all just cruise next to me (usually a little behind) and look. Sorta like when I had my Yamaha V-Max. I never had any kid on a crotch rocket even try to race me. They all knew I was the king of the road. They would just cruise next to me and nod their approval. <P>Walk softly and carry a big stick. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||rogergarrison||03-14-2001||06:41 AM||||True Rodney. Ive had the very few that made the mistake of trying to intimidate me though. A lot of people have the misconception from all the movies, that Lambos and Ferraris are supposed to be so powerful they blast off like the space shuttle. Thats not the way the european makers think. My AMG Mercedes would barely even chirp the tires, but above 40 mph it flew. It would kick down to 2nd gear at just under 100mph. US makers strive for torque, euros use revs to achieve what they need. Thats why the US cars were called 'muscle cars'.Most US street cars peak at around 5500 rpm while Porsche and Ferrari are near 9,000 rpm.||||reg||1
Z||000019||danny boy||03-14-2001||09:02 PM|||| Chrysler and Mitsubishi did a joint venture here and built the Talon/Eclipse/Laser., and I think the Galant.It was called Diamond-Star Motors. My Stealth was a Japan-built car, then Chrysler Corp. designed and installed the Front and rear fascias and sideskirts,steering wheels,and wheels here. I think thats how it happened. DSMs aren't really that popular in Japan.  <BR>   Somewhere I heard that Stealth/3000GT/GTO was based on the DSM cars.My girlie has an Eclipse and I can't find any similarities.The fuses and the overhead console lights are the same but thats it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Dumba$$||03-14-2001||09:11 PM||||speed, before looks anyday!!!<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE||||reg||1
Z||000021||Dumba$$||03-14-2001||09:15 PM||||hey danny boy,<BR>go look in an avenger, or stratus,<BR>they have the same guages as a mitsubishi<BR>and even have a mutsubishi  motor & symbol on the key<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||WKDFIRO||03-15-2001||12:52 PM||||Sometimes these ventures can produce some pretty nice cars like the later year Mazda Probe. The styling was nice and it had a nice DOHC V6 in it. But that was before their venture ended...||||reg||6
Z||000023||rogergarrison||03-15-2001||02:18 PM||||the 3000gt and stealth share components<P>the laser/eclipse/talon are all the same but different from 3000 and stealth. The only things different are lights and minor trim.<P>i like the stealth and 3000gt, there cool for japanese cars...which I generally hate.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy<BR><B> Chrysler and Mitsubishi did a joint venture here and built the Talon/Eclipse/Laser., and I think the Galant.It was called Diamond-Star Motors. My Stealth was a Japan-built car, then Chrysler Corp. designed and installed the Front and rear fascias and sideskirts,steering wheels,and wheels here. I think thats how it happened. DSMs aren't really that popular in Japan.  <BR>   Somewhere I heard that Stealth/3000GT/GTO was based on the DSM cars.My girlie has an Eclipse and I can't find any similarities.The fuses and the overhead console lights are the same but thats it.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||DL10||03-15-2001||05:23 PM||||I wanted to have somethng diferent. If I were building a kit I would do a motor swap first. I bought my car as a turnkey with a V-6. There is a V-8 comming in the furure<P>------------------<BR> DL10 Predator        <IMG SRC="http://chicagolandreplicar.tripod.com/_borders/LC_DB1_1.gif">     <BR>     <A HREF="mailto:dbagwell1@Prodigy.net">dbagwell1@Prodigy.net</A>       <A HREF="http://pages.prodigy.net/dbagwell1" TARGET=_blank>http://pages.prodigy.net/dbagwell1</A>||||reg||1
Z||000025||87GT||03-15-2001||09:04 PM||||The only time I have a problem with a kit car fiero is when it is done on a fiero that is in mint condition or done to a fiero from 1988. A few months back, a man bought a 88GT with real low miles on it and it was in mint condition, he came on here to the forum trying to trade it to anyone with a 88GT(in rough shape) for theirs plus $5000!!  It was a joke and everyone knew it, so he pretty much said he was gonna just cut it up and turn it into a kit car.  Pissed me off.  Im sure other forum members remember this. Im not a kit car fan, but I definately respect all the work people put into them.  I love the stock fiero looks for the most part.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||mshill||03-15-2001||11:30 PM||||I am building an F50 look-a-like (not stretched) because I love the look of the car.  The intention (at least mine) is not to make an exact replica of a Ferrari but to make it unique so it will be MY CAR.  All said and done I will have around $12K into it (including the 3.4L V6) when completed and will drive it daily during the spring and summer.  Like someone said earlier, I will have a lot more fun driving my kit than I would driving my Taurus (yes I have one).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||Spyder||03-16-2001||05:33 PM||||I wish I would have built my car first, then put the big engine in it later, because I would be out driving right now.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Spydersf355.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.markalexandermiller.com/carenginea.JPG"> <BR>I'm having the car painted this next month!!!! <BR>Just in time to miss the Daytona show. Darn it.<BR>||||reg||14
